{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465366-creating-a-baali-in-v5-homebrew-ideas","id":1465366,"title":"Creating a Baali in v5 Homebrew ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-26T00:48:48-07:00","id":1465366,"title":"Creating a Baali in v5 Homebrew ideas","content":"So i got myself into another V5 campaign this time the ST is fine with me creating a Baali character but i need to flesh out the rules on how that would work so id love to get your help, critique and input.<br /> <br /> I think the biggest thing to tackle here is also the most difficult - humanity. The rest i already mentioned in the &quot;review&quot; of the Baali guide,<br /> <br /> I hoped that the companion book that shows us how Tzimisce can be played under these rules, would bring paths back...well it didnt. It inerted a cheat code. Basicly you can do the most horrific things to little children without loosing humanity at all if they volunteer to being victims....and dominating themactually counts as volunteering which meens with but 1 dot dominate you can now cheat that any action you do, no matter how disgusting and evil, doesnt get to your humanity.<br /> <br /> Im not a fan of that at all, its just cheating around the issue and basicly makes the Tzmisce immune from consequences. Hence i looked at the various typical paths for Baali and try to distill down a working system, so that the Baali has to abide by rules (or suffer the consequences just with humanity rating)<br /> On that note im also not a fan of how humanity works in v5 cause it basicly makes human interaction impossible for older vampires, which we regularely witness to be broken in the canon (Helena as example) and ofc older vampires would just be mindless beasts and not scheming intelligent creatures...<br /> <br /> Now technicly each subtype of Baali would of course follow a different path, but for simplicity and applying to v5 i think its best to distill it down as much as possible and allow for an alternate option<br /> <br /> In V5 humanity is also very vague so start and its not actually said what actions lead to a decrease. Killing is bad sure....what about self defense? What if i dominate the target to hold still for a second? is that voluntary? Or as Smiling Jack said in Bloodlines &quot;...skin him, drain him dry and bash in his skull...its my favorite part of humanity&quot; ...well if you are threatened. Still it sounds like way over the top violence for self preserverance...but apparently that is human after all.<br /> <br /> So ill compare to the road of humanity in V20 <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_article-table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">10</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Selfish thoughts.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Thought is as good as deed</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Minor selfish acts.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Compassion separates us from the beasts</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Injury to another person (deliberate or otherwise).</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Follow the golden rule</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Theft and robbery.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Respect the property of others</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Accidental violation (e.g. drinking a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vessel_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">Vessel</a> dry from starvation).</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Ignorance does not excuse cruelty</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Wanton destruction.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Man creates; the beast destroys</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Impassioned violation (e.g. manslaughter, killing a vessel in <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Frenzy_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">Frenzy</a>).</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Those who act as beasts become beasts</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Planned violation (e.g. murder).</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">If you surrender to the beast, you become its slave</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Casual violation (e.g. wanton killing, feeding past satiation).</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Others are worthy of respect</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">The most heinous and demented acts.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Are you man or beast?</td> </tr> </table></div> (Taken from the official wiki)<br /> <br /> I guess this represents the humanity in v5 rather well, in special with the &quot;via&quot;s that exist that replace some tennets with others so that you actually can steal without loosing humanity but have to do your evry best to appear human all the time instead<br /> <br /> So based on this we can proceed forward and look at existing paths like Path of the Hive <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_article-table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">10</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Arguing with another follower of the Road or your Nest.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Joining forces with an outsider against a follower of the Road or your Nest.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Acting on impulse.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Actively working against a member of your Nest.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Betrayal of someone who could benefit the Nest.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Feeding from innocents with force.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Withholding knowledge from the Nest or betraying a member another <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Baali\" target=\"_blank\">Baali</a>.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Acting for any cause that does not benefit the Nest.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Betraying an Elder of the Road.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Betraying your sire or one to whom you are bound.</td> </tr> </table></div> or path of caine <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_article-table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">10</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Failing to research or study.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">The search for truth requires dedication.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Failing to teach another vampire about the Path.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">All vampires must have the opportunity to explore their potential.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Treating mortals as equals.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Caine was separated from mortals; as all vampires should be.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Disrespecting other students of Caine.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">All of the Children of Caine deserve the respect due their heritage, as long as they strive to understand themselves.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Failing to &quot;ride the wave&quot; of a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Frenzy_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">Frenzy</a>.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Direct the Beast; don't be directed by it.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Succumbing to <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/R%C3%B6tschreck\" target=\"_blank\">R\u00f6tschreck</a>.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Master your fear. Terror is for lesser beings.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Failing to <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Diablerie_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">diablerize</a> a &quot;humane&quot; vampire.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Those who don't explore their potential forfeit that potential.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Not testing the limits of your condition.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Develop your capabilities to their limits in order to discern your true nature.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Failing to pursue knowledge about Caine and vampirism.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Every scrap of knowledge adds a piece to the puzzle of undead existence.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Denying your hunger or other parts of the vampiric condition.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">To be a vampire, one must satisfy a vampire's needs.</td> </tr> </table></div> Or path of evil revelations <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_article-table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">10</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Maintaining a semblance of goodness.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Feign goodness but never presume that you are anything more than a servant of greater Evil.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Missing a nightly devotion or ritual.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Proper service requires constant affirmation.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Helping others without gaining an advantage.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Compassion and aid are simply tools to bring others into your debt.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Not using an opportunity to gain temporal power.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Power in the material world is the means by which the will of the infernal lords is expressed.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Following your own interests.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">The master's will is more important than one's own.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Not working with other servants of your Master.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">The master's goals are best served with unity against one's opponents.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Failing to fulfill your Masters agenda.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Advance the will of your lords whenever possible.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Providing secrets of the Infernal to outsiders.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Never reveal to outsiders your master's true motives, so that your master can't be fought.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Failing to destroy or corrupt another vampire.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">All vampires must recognize their proper place as agents of Evil or be destroyed.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Disobeying your Master.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">You must serve the interests of your superiors in Evil.</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> So this can give us a good idea how to judge actions done by the character, that come with drawbacks, and could replace the humanity mechanic but still keep the spirit of it. Any ideas on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 10-26-2021, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T01:04:40-07:00","id":1465367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In V5 humanity is also very vague so start and its not actually said what actions lead to a decrease. Killing is bad sure....what about self defense? What if i dominate the target to hold still for a second? is that voluntary? Or as Smiling Jack said in Bloodlines &quot;...skin him, drain him dry and bash in his skull...its my favorite part of humanity&quot; ...well if you are threatened. Still it sounds like way over the top violence for self preserverance...but apparently that is human after all. </div> </div> </div>I think this misunderstands Humanity. Humanity in V5 is only an automatic loss if you Embrace someone, diablerize someone, have your Touchstone damaged, or use certain Disciplines (which is stupid).<br /> <br /> Your Convictions can be monstrously evil.<br /> <br /> * Do not suffer a Catholic to live<br /> * Do not suffer disrespect<br /> * Revenge any slight","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T01:13:51-07:00","id":1465368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess this represents the humanity in v5 rather well </div> </div> </div>I think you are getting too hung up on the old rules. Humanity in V5 is much more flexible and much more meta. It is chiefly defined by: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>GM's opinion</li> <li>Chronicle Tenets</li> <li>Personal Convictions</li> </ol><br /> In a chronicle with the Humanist tenets dominating people to do dirty work for you would clearly be against the spirit of the game, and ding your Humanity. In a chronicle where you want to roleplay Camarilla's Camarilla dominating others to do your dirty work would be a chief virtue.<br /> <br /> Then you build your personal path via Convictions. Let's say you are a Baali on the Path of Screams. You might take convictions &quot;You are Damned; the greatest pleasure is found in service of Hell.&quot;, &quot;Always ride the wave of Frenzy - the Beast is the clarion call of your soul.&quot;, and &quot;Never be altruistic. You owe others nothing.&quot;<br /> Your Convictions will protect your Humanity when you do something ordered by demons, when you do something while riding the wave, and when you act like a selfish jerk. They will harm your humanity if you ignore the orders of hell, try to control the beast, or act out of the goodness of your heart.<br /> <br /> Humanity works just fine in V5. But you shouldn't be trying to rules lawyer tenets and convictions and seek loopholes in the exact words. They are a thing negotiated with the group. It's for everyone's fun, trying to be a smartass just makes you annoying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T08:14:31-07:00","id":1465405,"title":"","content":"The easy way to do Paths in V5 (if you don't want to use The Long Road out of Hell)? <br /> <br /> 1. Look up the V20 (or V20DA) Ethics for your chosen Path (or Road). These become your Convictions. Narrow them down if there are too many (some can be merged or abandoned).<br /> 2. Allow non-human Touchstones. The character starts with one less dot in &quot;Humanity&quot; for each non-human Touchstone they have (a quick fix, though TLRooH's Beast Marks are very cool).<br /> 3. If you want to replace the auto-Humanity-loss rules, you could do worse than just taking the bottom three Sins from your chosen Path and saying if you break any of those, you lose a point automatically.<br /> 4. Remove access to the benefits of higher level Humanity like Blush of Life, eating food and having sex. Most Paths won't have these, but it's okay because they're not things those vampires care about. The ST might let you use the Bearing rules if you want, but you'll need to convert the bonuses over. You get all the penalties, as usual.<br /> <br /> Hey presto. It's done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T09:12:46-07:00","id":1465411,"title":"","content":"My suggestion for Baali:<br /> <br /> Player and ST discuss 3 <i>Baali Tenets </i>for the chronicle. The Baali character gets to ignore the normal Chronicle Tenets and the normal rules for instant Humanity Loss, but in exchange the <i>Baali Tenets</i> ARE instant Humanity Loss. They should preferably be based on the most iconic and/or easy to follow tenets of the intended Path, although one of them can be just something for ease of play, like not betraying the group or something. YMMV.<br /> <br /> You get your personal Convictions as normal, although you may want to base at least one of them on your take on infernalism/demonology.<br /> <br /> Touchstones are the biggest change, being based on your personal approach to the infernal. A book, an artifact, the name of a demon, and so on. If it is a person, their role as touchstone is defined by their value to the Infernal, their service to a demon, or by the risk they're under (it is not about keeping them &quot;pure&quot;, but about avoiding/guaranteeing their literal damnation).<br /> <br /> \u200bIt is all very similar to what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5291\" data-vbnamecard=\"5291\">adambeyoncelowe</a> said, but I slept at the keyboard while writing and didn't got to post it soon enough, but more importantly it really seems like you read the rules on V5 keeping a little too much from the old rules on your head. Touchstones particularly, while most people agree the rule was poorly written, but I don't get how you went full on &quot;elders can't interact with humans&quot;. I suggest you clear your mind and reread that section again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T10:58:57-07:00","id":1465422,"title":"","content":"So for touchstones i had the idea of them being demonicly posessed humans that the Baali may or may not have had a hand creating. If one of them dies, the released demon will surely not be pleased and may act against the Baali before being sucked into the Abyss again?<br /> <br /> Could also be D'habi revenants or ghouls that the Baali is supposed to protect or maybe they provide vital services like collecting corpses for the well, and keeping ritual sites clean etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T11:35:49-07:00","id":1465425,"title":"","content":"I think those may work for a given character.<br /> <br /> The point of the new Humanity system is for it to be customized to your character, that's why bringing previous editions assumptions don't work. Keep it that way.<br /> <br /> As for Touchstones, most people already houserule them and make non-human Touchstones. What is important in any case is how you define <b>Harming</b> and <b>Destroying</b> a Touchstone. Indeed, most arguments against the rule are solely due to how those two things were defined in the core book.<br /> <br /> But it is simple. You suffer 1 stain if a Touchstone is harmed, 2 stains if it is destroyed, +1 if you were personally responsible for this. If you lose a Touchstone and don't replace it, one of your personal Convictions goes with them, those personal convictions being the thing that can help you staving off Humanity loss.<br /> <br /> For the possessed humans, you could define that your Touchstones are the possessing demons and they get Harmed when seriously impeded or destroyed if banished back to Hell, and for this Touchstone renewing it is always possible but necessarily entails summoning the same demons back. How those demons hold your Convictions is up to you.<br /> <br /> D'habi could work as normal Touchstones, or you could tie the Touchstone to their role instead of their persons, harming it when the work is delayed and destroying when it is seriously compromised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}